 - E5's verdict on a shape with optional flex is the drawing pipeline `DrawPlanarPipeline` (D422, amends D419; `PlanarDrawPipelineOptions` defaults): a seed; discovery rounds (at most 8, pairwise keep-apart with directions from the previous drawing (D418), `sep_extremal`, insert prices 0.05 in round 1 then 0.1 / (previous length + 0.5), box price 0.01, elastic on `sep`, stop after two slack-0 rounds); commit of the inserts at or above 1 half tile in the last discovery drawing (curve rows on them, the rest held at 0) with up to 4 rounds elastic on `sep` and `curve`; a prune holding at 0 the committed inserts whose `curve flex` rows still stretch, then up to 4 rounds again (`prunes`, default 1: repeated while a prune holds any); a prune whose rounds are not Optimal is undone (its inserts restored) and the final runs from the drawing before it; the slack price is `discovery_slack_price` for the seed and discovery rounds and `slack_price` from the commit on, both default 1; an integer final on the sides the last Optimal round proved (its input drawing, never re-read from a round's rounded output). Probes: `prunes` (default 1) and `additions` (default false: one additions pass after the prune, the committed inserts kept and the others free under IRL1 (`PlanarDrawOptions::curve_flex_free`), its used inserts committed, then the commit rounds and the prunes again). `curve_discovery` (on by default, D425, CARD-E5-schemeA): from discovery round 2 every insert is a real bend in the curve rows, those rows elastic at a price following a damped memory of the insert's length, at most 4 rounds after round 1. The corridor family is on in every stage (`corridor`; a beside track's parent chain is concatenated with a node's piece once: equal headings mod 8 across a join merge into one piece and one vertex, as H8); `keep_apart` (default true) is a pipeline option; the T1 test runs the defaults (keep-apart on). E5's verdict is the LP rounds (D423, restoring D419): the integer final has no tile-grid rows by default and its drawing is off the game grid, so it is a probe, not a gate; whole-tile grid integrality is Slots'.
 - Pins (D393, `PlanarDrawPins`, `ParsePlanarDrawPins`, `PlanarDrawOptions::pins`): the answer key's points (`end <line> start|end X Y`, `cross <a> <b> X Y`, half tiles, map frame, by track name) are held within a window of 2 half tiles per axis, up to one common shift (two free integer variables). The rows are hard (tag `pin end <line> start|end`, `pin cross <a> <b>`), no slack even in elastic mode; names the map lacks go to `unmatched`. D412: a port line with no crossing event (its stretch from the port to its first node is the whole line) may have total length 0, its pieces free (as a flex group's pieces are) and no least-length row for its flex groups.
 - Grid probe (`PlanarDrawOptions::grid`, pipeline `final_grid`, off by default): every point of an axis run of positive length is odd across it; the parities the integer equalities then force are propagated, each forced variable is written 2 h + p, and every all-integer row is divided by its gcd with its bounds rounded inward. On PSG 197 it forces 1240 variables and tightens 1045 rows, the root LP stays 1804.25, and no grid drawing is found in 15 s. `elastic_integer`, `final_soft_sep` and `final_soft_all` are its diagnostics (grid rows never get slack).
-- Sibling lanes (`PlanarDrawOptions::sibling_lanes`, pipeline `sibling_lanes`, off by default, a probe; D388 spine, SPEC-slots-lengths §11): per pair of lines of one channel (`PlanarSpinePairs(map, structure, true)`, every pair, same crossing sequence) that has two or more channel crossings with only channel crossings between the first and last, one non-zero equal side `s` over the interior stretches, and equal headings mod 8 and flex middles on the pieces of that range, the second line is the first one's offset curve one lane to side `s`: at each vertex of the range, for each heading of its two pieces, `STEP[(h + 2) % 8] . (point[b] - point[a]) == 2 s`, and at the range's two ends the end piece's normal only (tag `lane <a> <b> <i>`, hard in every stage after the seed; the seed's elastic-all mode softens it). Other pairs are skipped with a reason (`lane_skipped`) and get no fallback. Keep-apart skips the wall pairs of a used pair inside the range (`lane_sep_skipped`).
+- Sibling lanes (`PlanarDrawOptions::sibling_lanes`, pipeline `sibling_lanes`, off by default, a probe; D388 spine, SPEC-slots-lengths §11): per pair of lines of one channel (`PlanarSpinePairs(map, structure, true)`, every pair, same crossing sequence) that has one or more channel crossings with only channel crossings between the first and last, over the stretches from the one ending at the first crossing to the one starting after the last (paired by position) at least one non-zero side and all non-zero ones equal (`s`), and equal headings mod 8 and flex middles on the pieces of the crossing range, the second line is the first one's offset curve one lane to side `s`. The range extends backward and forward while the next pieces of both have equal headings mod 8 and flex membership and neither track has an event on them. At each vertex of the extended range, for each heading of its two pieces, `STEP[(h + 2) % 8] . (point[b] - point[a]) == 2 s`, and at the range's two ends the end piece's normal only (tag `lane <a> <b> <i>`, hard in every stage after the seed; the seed's elastic-all mode softens it). Other pairs are skipped with a reason (`lane_skipped`) and get no fallback. Keep-apart skips the wall pairs of a used pair inside the extended range (`lane_sep_skipped`). `lane_ranges` reads out per used pair its ranges before and after extension and its side.
 - Not yet in it: grid parity as a default (D382, D423), node legs to events, coverage, clearance against a box edge.
